# Access the PWA through a private VPN such as WireGuard or Tailscale.
# Replace the demonstration bearer tokens in docker-compose.yml before use.
# External model egress remains disabled unless a provider has been qualified.

# Release-manifest signature enforcement (optional in preclinical).
# Generate a keypair with the snippet in scripts/sign_release_manifest.py,
# sign the manifest, then point the relay at the trusted public-key map:
#   AI_DOCTOR_RELEASE_MANIFEST_PATH=/secure/path/release_manifest_v3.json
#   AI_DOCTOR_RELEASE_MANIFEST_PUBLIC_KEYS_JSON=/secure/path/manifest_keys.json
#   AI_DOCTOR_REQUIRE_SIGNED_MANIFEST=true
# With enforcement on, an unsigned or invalidly signed manifest refuses boot.
# Key rotation = publish a new key map (removing the old key revokes everything it signed) + re-sign.
